      {
        "dom_id": "question-73318",
        "name": "Question 6",
        "problem": "The area of a square decreases at a rate of $12\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}\\text{/min}.$ If $x$ and $A$ denote the side length and area of the square, respectively, then find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$, where $t$ is the time in minutes.",
        "worked_solution": "Here, the area is changing at a constant rate, and we want to know the rate at which the side lengths are changing.\n\nFirst, let's draw a diagram:\n\n![](images/f4/f4125cebd7553bb8b106a8baff39a6e4a120b9d9e5cdf2c4c9c0a9a676558897.png)\n\nWe want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ The area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know from the given information that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-12\\text{ in}{}^{2}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information, we reach\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{6}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields_complete": true,
        "result": "Correct",
        "html": "<div id=\"question-73318\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">6.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"73318\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The area of a square decreases at a rate of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"82\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-msup><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.396em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><msup><mtext>in</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>/min</mtext><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> If <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"83\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"84\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> denote the side length and area of the square, respectively, then find an expression for <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"85\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c64\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mrow></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c64\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mrow></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"86\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is the time in minutes.</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 10:13 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:15</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
