      {
        "dom_id": "question-344674",
        "name": "Question 20",
        "problem": "![](images/34/34a41e39a36d3e073ef2ca4144bd346b340efa22a9da7d3e8a9df48d32d900b3.png)\n\nA square opening in a testing chamber is being reduced, causing the area of the opening to decrease at a rate of $49{\\text{ mm}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$ At what rate are the diagonals decreasing when each diagonal measures $35\\,\\text{mm}?$\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of decrease is positive.\n\nThe diagonal is decreasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}} $\\text{mm/s}.$",
        "worked_solution": "Let $A$ be the area of the square opening, and $h$ be the length of its diagonal. The relationship between $A$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the relationship between $A$ and $h$ with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}h}(\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot h \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{h}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the area of the square is decreasing at a rate of $49{\\text{ mm}}^{2}\\text{/s},$ so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-49.\n$$\n\nAlso, we want to compute the rate of change of the diagonals when the diagonal has length $h=35.$ Substituting this information into our expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{35}\\cdot (-49) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{49}{35} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =-1.4\\text{ mm/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the diagonal of the opening is decreasing at a rate of \n$1.4\\text{ mm/s}.$",
        "problem_field_keys": [
          "field-1"
        ],
        "answer_fields_complete": true,
        "result": "Correct",
        "html": "<div id=\"question-344674\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">20.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"344674\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionGraphicFrame\"><img class=\"questionGraphic\" src=\"/graphics/q-344674\"></div><div class=\"questionText\">A square opening in a testing chamber is being reduced, causing the area of the opening to decrease at a rate of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"305\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msup><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cA0\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn><msup><mtext>&nbsp;mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>/s</mtext><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> At what rate are the diagonals decreasing when each diagonal measures <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"306\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6D\"></mjx-c