        ],
        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14210206/observations/step-e219-847dc431ca08669b1aaf.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14210206/observations/step-e219-847dc431ca08669b1aaf.png",
        "worked_solution": "This situation is different. Here, the *area* is changing at a constant rate,  and we want to know the rate at which the side lengths are changing.\n\nFirst, let's draw a diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14210206/assets/f4125cebd7553bb8b106a8baff39a6e4a120b9d9e5cdf2c4c9c0a9a676558897.png)\n\nWe want to find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$ The area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA = x^2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know from the given information that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-20\\text{ cm[math]^2[/math]/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information, we reach\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-20 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{10}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "can_dont_know": false,
        "can_skip": false,
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-e219",
          "name": "Example: Finding an Expression for the Rate of Change of a Side Length Given the Rate of Change of the Area",
          "problem": "The area of a square decreases at a rate of $20 \\text{ cm}^2\\text{/s}.$ If $x$ and $A$ denote the side length and area of the square respectively, then find an expression for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds.",
          "worked_solution": "This situation is different. Here, the *area* is changing at a constant rate,  and we want to know the rate at which the side lengths are changing.\n\nFirst, let's draw a diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14210206/assets/f4125cebd7553bb8b106a8baff39a6e4a120b9d9e5cdf2c4c9c0a9a676558897.png)\n\nWe want to find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$ The area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA = x^2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know from the given information that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-20\\text{ cm[math]^2[/math]/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information, we reach\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-20 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{10}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
          "fields": [],
          "problem_field_keys": [],
          "answer_fields_complete": null,
          "result": null,
          "proof_feedback": null,
          "html": "<div id=\"step-e219\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Finding an Expression for the Rate of Change of a Side Length Given the Rate of Change of the Area</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e219\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>The area of a square decreases at a rate of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"9.654ex\" height=\"3.009ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.838ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -934.9 4156.4 1295.7\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">20 \\text{ cm}^2\\text{/s}.</title>\n